# tests/mcp_protocol.rs compares this file byte-for-byte against what the
# server renders, which always uses LF. Without `-text`, a checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (default on Windows) reads the committed file back as
# CRLF, so the comparison fails on line endings alone rather than on any real
# schema drift. `-text` disables git's line-ending conversion for this path
# entirely, matching the LF the test always writes.
tests/snapshots/** -text
